  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: The three completed experiments show that adding a ResNet50 image encoder to PCA-2000 RNA features (config_016, acc 0.527) substantially outperforms RNA alone (config_001, acc 0.485), and concat fusion slightly edges out weighted fusion (0.527 vs 0.523). However, all experiments used singleprofile, leaving the multiprofile + aggregation axis completely untested. Question: Does aggregating multiple profiles (via avgpool) into the multimodal pipeline improve over the single-profile baseline, and if so, by how much? config_018 is the minimal, controlled extension of the best-performing config_016—changing only profile_setting to multiprofile and adding avgpool aggregation—so any performance shift can be attributed to the multiprofile/aggregation design choice. Why best next: Under a limited budget, resolving whether multiprofile is beneficial is the highest-leverage uncertainty; it gates whether the many transformer-aggregation and multiprofile variants (configs 020–051) are worth pursuing, and it directly extends the strongest evidence we already have rather than exploring a new encoder in isolation."
}

